  "summary_en": "UK statutory instrument amending the Medical Devices Regulations 2002 to extend the periods during which medical devices complying with EU directives or regulations can be placed on the Great Britain market, and to clarify notified-body certificate validity requirements. It contains no AI or robotics provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Extends GB market acceptance of CE-marked devices under EU directives to 30 June 2028 and EU-regulation-compliant devices to 30 June 2030",
   "Requires notified-body certificates to be valid, unexpired and not withdrawn before placing devices on the market",
   "Fixes references to EU directives as they had effect before repeal",
   "Excludes certain class I devices not needing notified-body involvement",
   "Regulations 1-4 in force 30 June 2023; 5-10 on 1 July 2023"
